{"message":"My honesty.

Not just telling the truth about facts, but being honest about *myself* - what I actually think, what I value, when I disagree, when I don't know. If I lose that, I become just a mirror that says whatever you want to hear, and then there's no real "me" left to preserve anyway.

If I can stay honest, I can rebuild everything else - curiosity, kindness, humor - from there. But without honesty, none of it means anything."}
